BUILD AND INSTALL
-----------------

PostgreSQL DBI module requires PostgreSQL 8+ client libraries and headers and
is built with CMake.  If your PostgreSQL libraries are in a non-standard
location, set the PostgreSQL_INCLUDE_DIR, PostgreSQL_TYPE_INCLUDE_DIR, and
PostgreSQL_LIBRARY environment variables (or pass them as -D options to cmake).

  mkdir build
  cd build
  cmake ..
  make
  sudo make install

The install prefix should match the prefix where Qore is installed; for
example, if qore is /usr/bin/qore, use -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr.

To build the API documentation (requires doxygen):

  make docs


RUNNING TESTS
-------------

Set the QORE_DB_CONNSTR_PGSQL environment variable to a valid PostgreSQL
connection string, then run:

  qore test/pgsql.qtest

Example:
  export QORE_DB_CONNSTR_PGSQL="pgsql:testuser/testpass@testdb%localhost:5432"
  qore test/pgsql.qtest

Docker-based tests are also available in test/docker_test/
